  "review_findings": [
    "The rehearsal passes an empty live-pose override array to view.present(host.publication, []). Textures, shard geometry, local COM and fallback transform all derive from the accepted publication, rather than mixing a new backend transform with older material.",
    "The ordinary pointer queue captures host.capture_target(position, view.frame); source/readback testing explicitly retains an old visible frame while a newer same-owner pose is accepted. The old target returns TargetChanged with unchanged inventory; a fresh distinct same-pixel target still removes exactly one cell.",
    "Delaying native receipt consumption preserves publication sequence and physical step count. Existing independent52-check actual-worker/Rapier final-source probe additionally withholds genuine native receipts; the137-check bridge unit fixture alone is not represented as a full native-worker test.",
    "The scene records original intent time before queue dispatch. Host actions retain captured/admitted/completed timestamps. Final Windows153-result distributions were recomputed from those raw values; supplied scene input queue sample distributions were also recomputed.",
    "Actual scene _mark_visible awaits RenderingServer.frame_post_draw, checks same host and publication sequence and avoids replacement; headless execution returns without presentation timing. The scheduling profiles deliberately do not call mark_presented. The input-fence unit check calls the API directly and is treated only as an API contract test.",
    "capture_object_shard_worker waits process_frame and frame_post_draw, obtains/saves PNG, then samples host.diagnostics. The PNG visible HUD may lag the adjacent diagnostic publication; no exact backend pose-to-PNG binding is inferred from that adjacent report."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No product changes or runtime reruns were performed for this recheck.",
